1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,529
Taxonomies categorize content items with terms.

2
00:00:04,529 --> 00:00:11,788
The Taxonomies Contents List Filters feature turns those terms into filters for the Content Items list.

3
00:00:11,788 --> 00:00:16,782
In this video, you enable it, choose the taxonomies to filter by, and

4
00:00:16,782 --> 00:00:18,780
filter the list by term.

5
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:27,642
A taxonomy is a set of terms that categorize content items, such as

6
00:00:27,642 --> 00:00:29,977
the Categories and Tags of a blog.

7
00:00:29,977 --> 00:00:33,948
As a site grows, so does the Content Items list, and the items

8
00:00:33,948 --> 00:00:36,750
that share one term are spread through it.

9
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,381
The Taxonomies Contents List Filters feature adds a button to the Content Items

10
00:00:42,381 --> 00:00:44,678
list for each taxonomy you choose.

11
00:00:44,678 --> 00:00:48,812
Pick a term from its dropdown, and the list shows only the content

12
00:00:48,812 --> 00:00:50,650
items that have that term.

13
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,020
Three steps set it up.

14
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:57,706
Enable the feature, choose the taxonomies to use as filters, and filter the

15
00:00:57,706 --> 00:01:00,020
Content Items list by their terms.

16
00:01:04,238 --> 00:01:05,906
Open Tools, Features.

17
00:01:05,906 --> 00:01:12,948
The Taxonomies Contents List Filters feature depends on the Taxonomies feature, which this site has enabled.

18
00:01:13,405 --> 00:01:15,587
Let's search for taxonomies.

19
00:01:15,587 --> 00:01:17,191
Two features match:

20
00:01:17,191 --> 00:01:23,544
Taxonomies is enabled, and Taxonomies Contents List Filters is disabled, with the description

21
00:01:23,544 --> 00:01:26,945
Provides taxonomy filters in the contents list.

22
00:01:27,399 --> 00:01:31,582
Select Enable on the Taxonomies Contents List Filters row.

23
00:01:31,582 --> 00:01:33,021
A message reads:

24
00:01:33,021 --> 00:01:37,139
The feature Taxonomies Contents List Filters was enabled.

25
00:01:41,332 --> 00:01:45,354
Open Settings, Taxonomy Filters, a page the feature adds.

26
00:01:45,354 --> 00:01:52,632
It needs the Manage settings and Manage taxonomies permissions, which the Administrator role has by default.

27
00:01:53,086 --> 00:01:57,338
The Taxonomies option lists the published taxonomies of the site.

28
00:01:57,338 --> 00:02:01,710
Each taxonomy you check becomes a filter in the Content Items list.

29
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:03,986
Let's check Categories and Tags.

30
00:02:04,450 --> 00:02:05,576
Select Save.

31
00:02:05,576 --> 00:02:06,953
A message reads:

32
00:02:06,953 --> 00:02:09,519
Site settings updated successfully.

33
00:02:09,519 --> 00:02:14,150
Clearing a checkbox and saving again removes that taxonomy's filter.

34
00:02:18,365 --> 00:02:20,469
Open Content, Content Items.

35
00:02:20,469 --> 00:02:25,544
The Manage Content page has a button for each taxonomy you chose, Categories

36
00:02:25,544 --> 00:02:29,505
and Tags, beside the Content Type, Show, and Sort filters.

37
00:02:29,965 --> 00:02:31,310
Open Categories.

38
00:02:31,310 --> 00:02:35,649
The dropdown is titled Filter by Categories and has a search box.

39
00:02:35,649 --> 00:02:40,478
It lists Clear filter, Show all, and the terms of the published taxonomy,

40
00:02:40,478 --> 00:02:43,595
with child terms indented below their parent.

41
00:02:44,055 --> 00:02:45,317
Choose Software.

42
00:02:45,317 --> 00:02:50,705
The page reloads, and the list shows only the content items that have the Software term.

43
00:02:51,156 --> 00:02:54,038
Open Categories again and choose Show all.

44
00:02:54,038 --> 00:02:58,181
The list shows every content item that has at least one term of

45
00:02:58,181 --> 00:03:03,706
this taxonomy, so items without a category, such as the About article, leave the list.

46
00:03:04,164 --> 00:03:09,514
Choose Clear filter to remove the Categories filter and bring back the full list.

47
00:03:09,972 --> 00:03:12,658
Each taxonomy has its own filter.

48
00:03:12,658 --> 00:03:18,442
Open Tags and choose Exploration to list the content items that have that tag.

49
00:03:22,653 --> 00:03:25,694
The taxonomy filters follow the content type.

50
00:03:25,694 --> 00:03:30,287
Open Content Type and choose Blog Post, a type that has taxonomy fields

51
00:03:30,287 --> 00:03:32,374
for both Categories and Tags.

52
00:03:32,374 --> 00:03:34,343
Both taxonomy buttons stay.

53
00:03:34,801 --> 00:03:36,511
Choose Article instead.

54
00:03:36,511 --> 00:03:40,756
The Article type has no taxonomy field, so neither button appears.

55
00:03:40,756 --> 00:03:45,060
When you choose a content type, a taxonomy filter shows only if the

56
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:47,831
type has a field that uses that taxonomy.

57
00:03:49,831 --> 00:03:54,950
The Taxonomies Contents List Filters feature turns the terms of your taxonomies into

58
00:03:54,950 --> 00:03:57,282
filters for the Content Items list.

59
00:03:57,282 --> 00:03:58,761
Thanks for watching.

